      "title": "Police search for clues to deadly shooting at Oregon elementary school",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/oct/16/oregon-school-shooting-latest",
      "description": "<p>Schools closed after one teacher and three children killed, and child and teacher hospitalized with critical injuries</p><p>Police are investigating a deadly shooting at an elementary school in Bend, Oregon, where a 16-year-old opened fire on Thursday, killing three children and a teacher, before being shot dead by an armed bystander.</p><p>Authorities in Oregon <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FPZBv81avCM\">said</a> that the three children killed at Silver Rail elementary school were aged five, eight and 11, and that a seven-year-old child and a 54-year-old teacher were also hospitalized with critical injuries.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/oct/16/oregon-school-shooting-latest\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-16T15:17:10"
    },
    {
      "title": "3 children, teacher killed in Oregon school shooting; shooter dead",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/3-children-teacher-killed-in-oregon-school-shooting-shooter-dead-126101600082_1.html",
      "description": "A 16-year-old opened fire at an elementary school in Bend, Oregon, on Thursday, killing three children and a teacher before he was shot by a person at the scene who pursued him into the school, authorities said.\nAuthorities found the suspect dead inside the school minutes after the shooting was first reported, Bend Police Chief Mike Krantz said.\nThe three children killed were aged 5, 8 and 11. Another child, 7, and a teacher, 54, were injured and taken to a hospital in critical condition, Krantz said.\nThe attacker, identified as a Bend resident, forced his way into the school by shooting at locked doors, police said. He was shot and went down inside the school shortly after officers arrived, police spokesperson Sheila Miller said.\nThe first 911 call came just before 1 pm from a person in a vehicle outside Silver Rail Elementary who reported being shot at by someone with a long gun, Krantz said.\nFurther 911 calls came from inside the school, and officers arrived on scene within ...",
